<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Impulse List vs Actual List
    </title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
</head>

<body>
    <section class="AddItem">
        <h1>Do you actually want to buy the thing, or is it just a fleeting desire?</h1>
        <!-- Browsers can only perform a CREATE (Think CRUD acronymn) operation if they send POST request to the server -->
        <!-- method tells browsers what kind of request to send, here we use POST because we're sending a POST request 
      action html attribute tells the browser where to send the POST request, here we're sending it to /quotes -->
        <div class="addItemForm">
            <form action="/addDocumentToWishListItemsCollection" method="POST">
                <div>
                <label name="itemName">What are you thinking about buying?</label>
                <input type="text" placeholder="Item" name="itemName" />
                </div>
                <div>
                <label name="itemURL">Link to the item</label>
                <input type="text" placeholder="Link" name="itemURL" />
                </div>
                <div>
                <label name="dateAddedToList">Record the date you had the impulse to buy the item</label>
                <input type="date" placeholder="Date" name="dateAddedToList" />
                </div>
                <button type="submit">Submit</button>
            </form>
        </div>
    </section>
    <section class="DisplayIndexEJS">
        <h2> Current Impulse List</h2>
        <p>This is when you added items that you were thinking about buying, the item and a link to the item. If it's
            been
            over 2 weeks or 14 days, review the items appearing, and determine if you still want them. If not, use the
            delete button to remove items older than 2 weeks. You've proven to yourself you don't need them!</p>
        <ul class="ImpulseListCollectionFromMongoDBcollectionNamedWishListItems">
            <!-- Loop through quotes objects from MongoDB -->
            <% for(let i=0; i < impulseList.length; i++) {%>
                <!-- output name from the iterated quote object. The name property on the quote object was defined above in the form. -->
                <li class="items">
                    <span data-msg-id="<%= impulseList[i]._id %>">
                        <%= impulseList[i].dateAddedToList %>
                    </span>
                    <span>
                        <%= impulseList[i].itemName %>
                    </span>
                    <a href="<%= impulseList[i].itemURL %>">
                        Check out the item!
                    </a>
                    </span>
                    <span><button class="trash">Delete Item</button></span>
                    <span><button class="moveItem">Move Item</button><span>
                            <!-- output quote from the iterated quote object. The quote property on the quote property was defined in the form above -->
                </li>
                <% } %>
        </ul>
    </section>
    <!-- We are going to use the button below to change something, our backend will handle an UPDATE operation, in the form of a PUT request. Extra information: like a POST request, PUT can be triggered either through Javascript or through a <form> element -->
    <section class="ActualWishList">
        <h2>Actual Wish List</h2>
        <p>If an item has been on the Current Impulse List for over 14 days, congradulations! Go ahead and move it to
            this list. You should budget, save and buy these things when you have enough cash!</p>
        <ul class="WishListCollectionFromMongoDBcollectionNamedWishListItems">
            <!-- Loop through quotes objects from MongoDB -->
            <% for(let i=0; i < wishList.length; i++) {%>
                <!-- output name from the iterated quote object. The name property on the quote object was defined above in the form. -->
                <li class="items">
                    <span data-msg-id="<%= wishList[i]._id %>">
                        <%= wishList[i].dateAddedToList %>
                    </span>
                    <span>
                        <%= wishList[i].itemName %>
                    </span>
                    <a href="<%= wishList[i].itemURL %>">
                        Check out the item!
                    </a>
                    <span><button class="trash">Delete Item</button></span>
                    <!-- output quote from the iterated quote object. The quote property on the quote property was defined in the form above -->
                </li>
                <% } %>
        </ul>
    </section>
